{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{artist: Sarah Adams & Lowell Mason}
{key: G}
{time: 6/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]Nearer, my [D]God, to [G]thee, [C]nearer to [D]thee!
[G]E'en though it [D]be a [Em]cross that [C]raiseth [D]me,
[G]still all my [D]song shall [G]be: nearer, my [C]God, to thee —
[G]nearer, my [C]God, to [D]thee, [G]nearer to [D]thee!

Verse 2
[G]Though like [D]the wanderer, [G]the [C]sun gone [D]down,
[G]Darkness be over [D]me, [Em]my rest [C]a [D]stone.
[G]Yet in my [D]dreams I'd [G]be nearer, [C]my God to Thee.
[G]Then evermore [C]to be [G]Nearer to [D]Thee!

Verse 3
[G]Nearer, my [D]Lord, [G]to [C]thee, [D]Nearer
[G]to thee! [D]Who [Em]to the [D]cross
[G]didst come, [D]Dying [G]for me! [C]Strengthen my willing
[G]feet, Hold [C]me [D]in [G]service [D]sweet

Verse 4
[G]Nearer, [D]O [G]Comforter, [C]Nearer [D]to
[G]thee! Who [D]with [Em]my loving [D]Lord
[G]Dwellest with [D]me! [G]Grant me [C]thy fellowship! Help
[G]me [C]each [D]day [G]to [D]keep

Verse 5
[G]But to [D]be [G]nearer [C]still, [D]Bring
[G]me, O [D]God, Not [Em]by [C]the [D]visioned
[G]steeps Angels [D]have trod. [G]Here where [C]thy cross I
[G]see, Jesus, [C]I [D]wait [G]for [D]thee,
